course: dictionary
lesson: 14510
title: Pennant
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pennant is a long, narrow flag shaped like a triangle. You can work out what it is from the words around it. «The school yard was full of pennants flapping in the wind.» Pennants flap like flags, and they are long and thin, so they are not like the big square flags you might see on a playground.
explain: People use pennants on ships, at sports grounds and for decoration. «At the birthday party, red and yellow pennants were strung across the garden.» Strung across the garden tells you they were hung up to make the party look bright and cheerful.
explain: In American baseball, a pennant means something more. «The team hoped to win the pennant this year.» Here, win the pennant means to be the best team in the league, and the flag marks that title. The word has more than one meaning, so always check the sentence to see which one fits.
fact: A pennant is a long, narrow flag shaped like a triangle.
fact: Pennants are used on ships, at sports grounds, at schools and as decoration.
fact: «Pennant» can also mean the title of the winner of a baseball league, and the flag that marks it.
fact: To win the pennant means to be the best team in a baseball league.
fact: Pennant is a noun, and its plural is pennants.
exercise: «The school yard was full of pennants flapping in the wind.» What is a pennant? | A kind of tall tree | A round ball used in sport | *A long, narrow triangle-shaped flag | A type of warm hat
exercise: «The team hoped to win the pennant this year.» In this sentence, what does win the pennant mean? | Lose every game and go home | *Be the best team in the league | Buy a new flag for the shop | Paint a picture of a ship
exercise: Which thing is a pennant most likely used for? | Carrying water up a hill | Cooking a dinner | *Decorating a birthday party | Keeping a bed warm
test: «The ship sailed out with a red pennant flying from its mast.» Where is the pennant? | Under the sea | Inside a shop window | *On the mast of a ship | Buried in the sand
test: Which of these words names a long, narrow flag shaped like a triangle? | pebble | *pennant | pelican | pillow
exam: «Ruby said the team needed one more win to take the pennant.» What does take the pennant mean here? | Plant a flag in the grass | Sell the flag at the shop | *Become the league winner | Lose the game badly
